      <location />
      <notes>Datachip: For occasions when you want to transfer data by physical means—like bringing the project specs on the competition’s new cyberdeck to Mr. Johnson in person at the meet—a datachip can hold enormous quantitites of data in a small finger-sized chip, accessible by any electronic device. Datachips have no wireless ca- pability, so you need to plug them into a universal data connector (found on any device) if you want to read or write to them.</notes>
      <notesColor>Chocolate</notesColor>
      <discountedcost>False</discountedcost>
